      "limitations": [
        "The independently inspected source3.12 market supplies milled loose quicklime. Its producer buys quicklime pieces from a calcination process. The native milled product likewise buys native quicklime pieces. Native2026 documentation explicitly includes calcination in vertical kilns; native2025 has the same inspected positive limestone, heavy-fuel-oil and fossil-CO2 coordinates. This is a complete calcined quicklime supply, not crushed limestone alone; do not extrapolate the older source3.9 loose-lime documentation defect to this release.",
        "Both source and native complete references are positive one kg. Preserve signed caller kg, marginal uncertainty and separate purchases at factor +1. Native CaO formula, actual calcination chain and named product establish the function; native CAS/synonym text is inconsistent and is retained as a documentation limitation. No inferred hydration, CaO-to-CaCO3, purity or second calcination multiplier is introduced.",
        "Use complete native Swiss loose quicklime as a screening proxy. Source global/Rest-of-World production mix, final delivery, kiln fuel, calcination emissions, allocation, processing, equipment life, internal uncertainty and mapped-biosphere exclusions differ, with unquantified score effects. No other version, reverse or consequential permission follows."
